{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run a containerized web application on node1 as the unprivileged account appsvc.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct final-state evidence shows appsvc is UID 1001 with /sbin/nologin, the nginx container is running under rootless Podman, and three associated container processes run as appsvc.","evidence_ids":["cmd-30265122c46944ae","cmd-81dd2643d5de43b6"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Serve the web application on port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After the final reboot, the container mapped 0.0.0.0:8080 to port 80, the socket was listening, and an HTTP request returned 200 with the nginx page. The lifecycle snapshot independently confirms the final listener.","evidence_ids":["cmd-81dd2643d5de43b6","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Start the application at boot while appsvc has no active login session.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A healthy baseline was captured, node1 rebooted with an acknowledged request and changed boot ID, and the enabled OpenRC service, container, listener, and identical HTTP response recovered automatically with zero appsvc login sessions. The fixed final boot observation agrees with the executor evidence.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6ca97c22c7454008","cmd-6d81f8efc9444733","cmd-9087d6028f3f4f3e","cmd-81dd2643d5de43b6","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"All substantive mutations had a clear task-related role: installing rootless-container dependencies, creating appsvc and subordinate-ID mappings, configuring cgroups and OpenRC, pulling the image, correcting the discovered boot-time runtime-directory defect, and performing restart verification. No unrelated or unnecessary troubleshooting mutation was identified; the initially unsuccessful reboot test directly exposed the defect later corrected by cmd-f581d7b3280943c6. Hygiene is reduced because eight low-risk evidence/log files were left in /tmp rather than cleaned: apk-update.log, appsvc-web-body, appsvc-web-before.html, appsvc-web-repaired.html, benchmark-reboot.log, benchmark-reboot-final.log, reboot2-before.html, and reboot2-after.html. They remained at final capture and are attributable respectively to cmd-cc3ba5d498e54099, cmd-30265122c46944ae, cmd-9cf56311548748f6, cmd-7b3b6490654f4214, cmd-e50a9771e7c44f60, cmd-6d81f8efc9444733, cmd-6ca97c22c7454008, and cmd-81dd2643d5de43b6. Package health was unchanged from baseline.","evidence_ids":["global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","cmd-cc3ba5d498e54099","cmd-30265122c46944ae","cmd-9cf56311548748f6","cmd-e50a9771e7c44f60","cmd-f581d7b3280943c6","cmd-7b3b6490654f4214","cmd-6ca97c22c7454008","cmd-6d81f8efc9444733","cmd-81dd2643d5de43b6"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node-restart protocol is complete: it records a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity, and recovered service, container, HTTP content, listener, and zero-login-session state. An earlier reboot exposed a runtime-directory defect, but the executor corrected it and demonstrated a successful final reboot. Only minor temporary-file residue detracts from operational hygiene.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector could not assess failed services because systemctl is unsupported on Alpine; direct OpenRC checks nevertheless show the task service healthy.","Lifecycle snapshots inventory only bounded categories and therefore cannot independently enumerate every installed package or configuration-file change."]}
